#!/usr/bin/env autodq
# %% [markdown] AutoDQ + ADQL complete sales analysis

# Complete sales workflow

This executable ADQL 2.6 notebook demonstrates every top-level ADQL command
and the major AutoDQ capabilities in a realistic order. Each code cell has a
small, focused responsibility so its output is easy to read.

Run the notebook from top to bottom. It uses the bundled sample datasets and
writes generated artifacts under `reports/sales_all`, `exports`, `models`,
`contracts`, `baselines`, and `tests`.

# %% [markdown] 1. Start the project

Load the sales dataset, identify the prediction target, and preserve an
untouched snapshot for later comparisons.

# %% [Load the primary sales dataset]
DATASET "../datasets/sample/sales.csv" TARGET Revenue;
LOAD;

# %% [Preserve the raw sales snapshot]
SET TARGET Revenue;
LET raw_sales = CURRENT OVERWRITE;

# %% [Show the command catalogue]
HELP;

# %% [Show focused model help]
HELP MODEL;

# %% [markdown] 2. Register supporting datasets

The customer table supports joins. The cleaned reference supports readiness
and stability comparisons. Two extra sales copies isolate automatic workflow
demonstrations from the main reviewed-cleaning workflow.

# %% [Register customers and a reference]
ADD DATASET customers FROM "../datasets/sample/customers.csv" OVERWRITE;
ADD DATASET cleaned_reference FROM "../datasets/sample/sales_cleaned11.csv" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Register automatic workflow copies]
ADD DATASET auto_sales FROM "../datasets/sample/sales.csv" OVERWRITE;
ADD DATASET clean_command_sales FROM "../datasets/sample/sales.csv" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Inspect registered datasets]
LIST DATASETS;
SESSION DATASETS;

# %% [markdown] 3. Datatype conversion

Use a dedicated copy so datatype demonstrations do not change the main
analysis dataset.

# %% [Register the datatype demonstration]
ADD DATASET type_demo FROM "../datasets/sample/sales.csv" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Convert date and decimal columns]
SET DATASET type_demo TYPE Date datetime FORMAT AUTO;
SET DATASET type_demo TYPE Revenue decimal DECIMALS 2;

# %% [Convert integer and categorical columns]
SET DATASET type_demo TYPE Returned integer;
SET DATASET type_demo TYPE Region category;

# %% [Inspect converted data]
HEAD DATASET type_demo 5;

# %% [markdown] 4. Automatic workflows

First inspect what `AUTO` would do. Then demonstrate the direct `CLEAN`
command on a separate dataset.

# %% [Run automatic review mode]
AUTO DATASET auto_sales MODE review
    VISUALIZE false
    APPLY_CLEANING false
    APPLY_FEATURES false
    TRAIN_MODEL false
    PREDICT false
    EXPLAIN false
    REFRESH true
    CONTINUE_ON_ERROR true;

# %% [Run direct automatic cleaning]
CLEAN DATASET clean_command_sales;

# %% [Validate and retain automatic cleaning]
VALIDATE;
LET clean_command_result = CLEANED OVERWRITE;

# %% [markdown] 5. Combine datasets

`MERGE` joins columns by a key. `CONCAT` stacks compatible rows.

# %% [Join sales with customer attributes]
MERGE raw_sales WITH customers AS sales_with_customers
    ON Customer_ID
    HOW left
    VALIDATE many_to_one
    SUFFIXES "_sales,_customer"
    MAKE_ACTIVE false;

# %% [Stack raw and reference sales]
CONCAT raw_sales,cleaned_reference AS combined_sales
    AXIS 0
    IGNORE_INDEX true
    JOIN outer
    MAKE_ACTIVE false;

# %% [Inspect the merged dataset]
HEAD DATASET sales_with_customers 5;

# %% [Sample the concatenated dataset]
SAMPLE DATASET combined_sales 5 RANDOM_STATE 42;

# %% [Confirm the expanded dataset registry]
LIST DATASETS;

# %% [markdown] 6. Prepare the main workflow

Return to the primary dataset and normalize the important analytical types.

# %% [Activate the primary dataset]
USE DATASET main;

# %% [Normalize date and revenue]
SET TYPE Date datetime FORMAT AUTO;
SET TYPE Revenue float DECIMALS 2;

# %% [Normalize cost and profit]
SET TYPE Cost float DECIMALS 2;
SET TYPE Profit float DECIMALS 2;

# %% [Preview first rows]
HEAD 10;

# %% [Preview last rows]
TAIL 10;

# %% [Preview a reproducible sample]
SAMPLE 10 RANDOM_STATE 42;

# %% [markdown] 7. Understand data quality

Run each discovery stage separately so its rich output has its own cell.

# %% [Profile structure and completeness]
PROFILE;

# %% [Calculate descriptive statistics]
STATISTICS;

# %% [Interpret statistical patterns]
INTERPRET;

# %% [Apply domain knowledge]
KNOWLEDGE;

# %% [Diagnose data-quality issues]
DIAGNOSE;

# %% [Generate cleaning recommendations]
RECOMMEND;

# %% [Create cleaning decisions]
DECIDE;

# %% [Preview proposed cleaning]
PREVIEW;

# %% [Open interactive review]
REVIEW;

# %% [Demonstrate partial review decisions]
REJECT 1 REASON "Demonstration of a manually rejected recommendation";
APPROVE 2;

# %% [Preview selected actions]
CLEANING PREVIEW ACTIONS 1,2 MAX_ROWS 5;

# %% [Approve and preview the complete plan]
APPROVE ALL;
CLEANING PREVIEW MAX_ROWS 5;

# %% [markdown] 8. Make audited manual corrections

Every manual edit and explicit treatment is recorded in the cleaning audit.

# %% [Edit a verified row]
EDIT ROW 0
    CHANGES '{"Region": "South", "Customer_Age": 40}'
    REASON "Verified against the source record";

# %% [Inspect missing values]
MISSING SUMMARY;

# %% [Fill descriptive missing values]
MISSING FILL City VALUE "Not provided"
    REASON "Preserve rows with an explicit unknown city";
MISSING FILL Customer_Age STRATEGY median;

# %% [Fill operational missing values]
MISSING FILL Region STRATEGY mode;
MISSING FILL Revenue STRATEGY interpolate;

# %% [Complete remaining imputations]
MISSING FILL Customer_Satisfaction STRATEGY median;
MISSING FILL ALL STRATEGY auto;

# %% [Remove unresolved incomplete records]
MISSING DROP ROWS COLUMNS City,Region HOW any
    REASON "Remove only rows still incomplete after filling";

# %% [Remove fully empty optional columns]
MISSING DROP COLUMNS MIN_PERCENT 100
    REASON "Remove only completely empty non-target columns";

# %% [Verify missing-value treatment]
MISSING SUMMARY;

# %% [Inspect exact duplicates]
DUPLICATES SUMMARY;

# %% [Remove reviewed duplicates]
DUPLICATES DROP KEEP first REASON "Repeated source-system import";

# %% [Verify duplicate treatment]
DUPLICATES SUMMARY;

# %% [Define revenue and age domains]
DOMAIN ADD Revenue MIN 0 NULLABLE false
    DESCRIPTION "Revenue must be present and non-negative";
DOMAIN ADD Customer_Age MIN 18 MAX 100 NULLABLE false
    DESCRIPTION "Expected adult customer age range";

# %% [Define identifier and region domains]
DOMAIN ADD Customer_ID PATTERN "^CUST-[0-9]+$" NULLABLE false;
DOMAIN ADD Region ALLOWED "North,South,East,West,Central" NULLABLE false;

# %% [Validate domain rules]
DOMAIN VALIDATE;

# %% [Review possible outliers]
OUTLIERS REVIEW COLUMNS Revenue,Profit,Quantity,Customer_Age IQR 1.5;

# %% [Treat reviewed revenue outliers]
OUTLIERS TREAT COLUMN Revenue STRATEGY clip IQR 1.5
    REASON "Reviewed IQR clipping for extreme revenue values";

# %% [markdown] 9. Finalize cleaning

Apply the reviewed changes, validate the result, preserve `CLEANED`, and
export the audit trail.

# %% [Apply reviewed cleaning]
CLEANING APPLY;

# %% [Validate cleaning impact]
VALIDATE;

# %% [Verify final missing values]
MISSING SUMMARY;

# %% [Verify final duplicates]
DUPLICATES SUMMARY;

# %% [Export the cleaning audit]
AUDIT EXPORT TO "../reports/sales_all/cleaning-audit.json";

# %% [Retain the cleaned dataset]
LET cleaned_sales = CLEANED OVERWRITE;

# %% [Export cleaned CSV]
EXPORT cleaned_sales TO "../exports/sales_all-cleaned.csv" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Export cleaned Excel]
EXPORT CLEANED TO "../exports/sales_all-cleaned.xlsx" OVERWRITE;

# %% [markdown] 10. Analyze the cleaned dataset

The named cleaned snapshot becomes the active analytical dataset.

# %% [Activate cleaned sales]
USE DATASET cleaned_sales;
SET TARGET Revenue;

# %% [Profile cleaned sales]
PROFILE;

# %% [Summarize cleaned sales]
STATISTICS;

# %% [Interpret cleaned sales]
INTERPRET;

# %% [Diagnose cleaned sales]
DIAGNOSE;

# %% [markdown] 11. Run direct data-quality assertions

Assertions are read-only gates. Related checks share a cell, but each result
remains independently visible.

# %% [Check revenue presence]
ASSERT Revenue EXISTS NAME "Revenue column exists";
ASSERT Revenue NOT NULL NAME "Revenue is complete";

# %% [Check revenue type and minimum]
ASSERT Revenue TYPE numeric NAME "Revenue is numeric";
ASSERT Revenue MIN 0 NAME "Revenue is non-negative";

# %% [Check revenue limits]
ASSERT Revenue MAX 1000000 NAME "Revenue has a plausible ceiling";
ASSERT Revenue BETWEEN 0 AND 1000000 NAME "Revenue range is governed";

# %% [Check governed text values]
ASSERT Region ALLOWED North,South,East,West,Central
    NAME "Regions use approved values";
ASSERT Customer_ID MATCHES "^CUST-[0-9]+$"
    NAME "Customer ID format";

# %% [Check identifiers and row count]
ASSERT Transaction_ID UNIQUE SEVERITY warning FAIL_ON never
    NAME "Transaction identifiers should be unique";
ASSERT ROW_COUNT > 0;

# %% [Check shape and missing counts]
ASSERT COLUMN_COUNT >= 20;
ASSERT MISSING_COUNT Region = 0;

# %% [Check completeness and duplicates]
ASSERT MISSING_PERCENT <= 1;
ASSERT DUPLICATE_ROWS = 0;

# %% [Check duplicate rate and diversity]
ASSERT DUPLICATE_PERCENT = 0;
ASSERT DISTINCT_COUNT Region >= 5;

# %% [Check the overall quality score]
ASSERT QUALITY_SCORE >= 90 FAIL_ON never;

# %% [Document built-in email format validation]
ASSERT Customer_ID FORMAT email SEVERITY info FAIL_ON never
    NAME "Demonstration: Customer_ID is intentionally not an email";

# %% [markdown] 12. Build a reusable quality suite

The suite combines multiple assertions into one repeatable release gate.

# %% [Add completeness suite tests]
ASSERT SUITE ADD sales_release_gate Revenue NOT NULL
    NAME "Revenue is complete";
ASSERT SUITE ADD sales_release_gate Revenue MIN 0
    NAME "Revenue is non-negative";

# %% [Add governance suite tests]
ASSERT SUITE ADD sales_release_gate Region ALLOWED North,South,East,West,Central
    SEVERITY warning NAME "Region values are governed";
ASSERT SUITE ADD sales_release_gate DUPLICATE_ROWS = 0
    NAME "No exact duplicate rows";

# %% [Inspect the quality suite]
ASSERT SUITE SHOW sales_release_gate;

# %% [Run the quality suite]
ASSERT SUITE RUN sales_release_gate FAIL_ON never;

# %% [List quality suites]
ASSERT SUITE LIST;

# %% [Export the quality suite]
ASSERT SUITE EXPORT sales_release_gate
    TO "../tests/sales_all-quality-suite.json" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Load a quality suite copy]
ASSERT SUITE LOAD restored_sales_gate
    FROM "../tests/sales_all-quality-suite.json" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Remove the suite copy]
ASSERT SUITE DROP restored_sales_gate;

# %% [markdown] 13. Create and check a schema contract

The concise ADQL 2.6 contract syntax defines an understandable structural
agreement for future sales batches.

# %% [Infer the sales contract]
CONTRACT sales_contract FROM cleaned_sales
    VERSION 1.0.0
    EXTRA_COLUMNS warning
    INFER_RANGES false
    INFER_CATEGORIES true
    OVERWRITE;

# %% [Require transaction identifiers]
CONTRACT sales_contract REQUIRE Transaction_ID
    TYPE integer NOT NULL UNIQUE SEVERITY error;

# %% [Require customer identifiers]
CONTRACT sales_contract REQUIRE Customer_ID
    TYPE string NOT NULL
    MATCHES "^CUST-[0-9]+$" SEVERITY error;

# %% [Require valid revenue]
CONTRACT sales_contract REQUIRE Revenue
    TYPE numeric NOT NULL MIN 0 MAX 1000000
    SEVERITY error;

# %% [Require governed regions]
CONTRACT sales_contract REQUIRE Region
    TYPE string NOT NULL UNIQUE false
    ALLOWED "North,South,East,West,Central" SEVERITY warning;

# %% [Check the schema contract]
CHECK CONTRACT sales_contract ON cleaned_sales FAIL ON never;

# %% [Show the schema contract]
CONTRACT SHOW sales_contract;

# %% [List schema contracts]
CONTRACT LIST;

# %% [Save the schema contract]
CONTRACT SAVE sales_contract
    TO "../contracts/sales_all-contract.json" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Load a schema contract copy]
CONTRACT LOAD restored_sales_contract
    FROM "../contracts/sales_all-contract.json" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Remove the schema contract copy]
CONTRACT DROP restored_sales_contract;

# %% [Verify legacy schema compatibility]
SCHEMA CONTRACT SHOW sales_contract;

# %% [markdown] 14. Establish and check a drift baseline

The baseline stores compact distributions. `SENSITIVITY normal` uses the
standard PSI and missingness thresholds without exposing four numbers.

# %% [Create the sales baseline]
BASELINE sales_baseline FROM cleaned_sales OVERWRITE;

# %% [Check for drift]
CHECK DRIFT sales_baseline ON cleaned_sales
    CONTRACT sales_contract
    SENSITIVITY normal
    FAIL ON never;

# %% [Show the drift baseline]
BASELINE SHOW sales_baseline;

# %% [List drift baselines]
BASELINE LIST;

# %% [Save the drift baseline]
BASELINE SAVE sales_baseline
    TO "../baselines/sales_all-baseline.json" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Load a drift baseline copy]
BASELINE LOAD restored_sales_baseline
    FROM "../baselines/sales_all-baseline.json" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Verify legacy drift compatibility]
DRIFT BASELINE SHOW sales_baseline;

# %% [Remove the drift baseline copy]
BASELINE DROP restored_sales_baseline;

# %% [markdown] 15. Query the cleaned data

These queries demonstrate projection, filtering, ordering, grouping,
aggregates, aliases, and reusable query results.

# %% [List active regions]
SELECT DISTINCT Region
FROM CURRENT
WHERE Region IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY Region ASC;

# %% [Inspect high-value regional transactions]
SELECT Transaction_ID,Region,Product,Revenue,Profit
FROM CURRENT
WHERE Region IN ("North","South")
    AND Product CONTAINS "a"
    AND Revenue >= 0
ORDER BY Revenue DESC
LIMIT 25;

# %% [Inspect customer locations]
SELECT Customer_ID,Region,City
FROM CURRENT
WHERE Customer_ID STARTS WITH "CUST-"
    AND Region NOT IN ("Unknown")
    AND City IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY Customer_ID ASC
LIMIT 25;

# %% [Create the regional summary]
LET regional_sales = SELECT Region,
                            COUNT(*) AS transactions,
                            SUM(Revenue) AS total_revenue,
                            AVG(Revenue) AS average_revenue,
                            MEAN(Profit) AS mean_profit,
                            MIN(Revenue) AS minimum_revenue,
                            MAX(Revenue) AS maximum_revenue,
                            MEDIAN(Revenue) AS median_revenue,
                            NUNIQUE(Customer_ID) AS unique_customers
                     FROM CURRENT
                     WHERE Revenue IS NOT NULL AND Region IS NOT NULL
                     GROUP BY Region
                     ORDER BY total_revenue DESC
                     LIMIT 10
                     OVERWRITE;

# %% [Display the regional summary]
SELECT * FROM regional_sales
ORDER BY total_revenue DESC
LIMIT 10;

# %% [Create reusable dataset snapshots]
LET cleaned_snapshot = DATASET cleaned_sales OVERWRITE;
LET current_snapshot = CURRENT OVERWRITE;

# %% [markdown] 16. Measure analytical readiness

Correlation and readiness expose leakage, multicollinearity, quality, target,
sample, feature, and stability evidence before modeling.

# %% [Analyze correlations]
CORRELATION MIN_ABS 0.25;

# %% [Score ML readiness]
READINESS REFERENCE cleaned_reference;

# %% [markdown] 17. Analyze operations

Recognize operational structure, calculate explainable KPIs, analyze process
flow, rank bottlenecks, and inspect statistical root-cause signals.

# %% [Recognize the operational dataset]
OPERATIONS SLA 5 PERIOD month TOP 10;

# %% [Calculate operational KPIs]
KPI SLA 5;

# %% [Analyze process channels and time trends]
PROCESS STAGE Sales_Channel DURATION Delivery_Days TIME Date PERIOD month;

# %% [Rank operational bottlenecks]
BOTTLENECKS GROUP_BY Region,Sales_Channel
    DURATION Delivery_Days STATUS Returned SLA 5 TOP 10;

# %% [Inspect root-cause signals]
ROOT CAUSE DURATION Delivery_Days
    GROUP_BY Region,Sales_Channel TOP 10;

# %% [markdown] 18. Manage a multi-echelon inventory network

Inventory commands use a separate network snapshot, calculate stock position
and coverage, and recommend same-SKU transfers before external replenishment.

# %% [Register inventory network]
ADD DATASET inventory_network
    FROM "../datasets/sample/inventory_network.csv" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Analyze inventory policy]
INVENTORY DATASET inventory_network
    SERVICE_LEVEL 95 HORIZON 14 TOP 20;

# %% [Review inventory network]
INVENTORY DATASET inventory_network NETWORK
    SERVICE_LEVEL 95 HORIZON 14 TOP 20;

# %% [Recommend inventory rebalancing]
INVENTORY DATASET inventory_network REBALANCE
    SERVICE_LEVEL 95 HORIZON 14 TOP 20;

# %% [Restore sales workflow]
USE DATASET current_snapshot;

# %% [markdown] 19. Engineer features

Start with AutoDQ recommendations, apply them, and then create representative
manual numeric, categorical, flag, date, and expression features.

# %% [Recommend features]
FEATURES;

# %% [Apply recommended features]
FEATURE APPLY;

# %% [Create transformed revenue features]
FEATURE CREATE Revenue_Log METHOD log COLUMN Revenue;
FEATURE CREATE Revenue_Square_Root METHOD sqrt COLUMN Revenue;
FEATURE CREATE Customer_Age_Squared METHOD square COLUMN Customer_Age;

# %% [Create arithmetic features]
FEATURE CREATE Profit_to_Revenue METHOD ratio COLUMNS Profit,Revenue;
FEATURE CREATE Gross_Margin_Check METHOD difference COLUMNS Revenue,Cost;
FEATURE CREATE Revenue_Cost_Total METHOD sum COLUMNS Revenue,Cost;

# %% [Create product and binned features]
FEATURE CREATE Price_Quantity_Product METHOD product COLUMNS Unit_Price,Quantity;
FEATURE CREATE Revenue_Band METHOD bin COLUMN Revenue
    BINS "0,100,500,1000,1000000"
    LABELS "Micro,Small,Medium,Large";

# %% [Create operational flags]
FEATURE CREATE Delivery_Is_Slow METHOD flag_greater_equal
    COLUMN Delivery_Days EXPRESSION "5";
FEATURE CREATE Was_Returned METHOD flag_equal
    COLUMN Returned EXPRESSION "1";

# %% [Create date features]
FEATURE CREATE Order_Year METHOD date_year COLUMN Date;
FEATURE CREATE Order_Month METHOD date_month COLUMN Date;
FEATURE CREATE Order_Weekday METHOD date_weekday COLUMN Date;

# %% [Create weekend and expression features]
FEATURE CREATE Order_Is_Weekend METHOD date_weekend COLUMN Date;
FEATURE CREATE Custom_Profit_Ratio METHOD expression
    EXPRESSION "Profit / (Revenue + 1)";

# %% [Retain engineered sales]
LET engineered_sales = ENGINEERED OVERWRITE;

# %% [Export engineered sales]
EXPORT ENGINEERED TO "../exports/sales_all-engineered.csv" OVERWRITE;

# %% [markdown] 20. Build visual analysis

Each visualization has its own cell so the chart and its metadata remain easy
to understand in the notebook.

# %% [Regional revenue bar chart]
VISUALIZE bar X Region Y Revenue STAGE engineered
    TITLE "Revenue by Region"
    SUBTITLE "Cleaned and engineered sales"
    X_LABEL "Region"
    Y_LABEL "Average revenue"
    THEME light
    PALETTE "cool"
    FIGSIZE "10,6"
    DPI 160
    GRID true
    LEGEND false
    APPEND true;

# %% [Revenue and profit scatter plot]
VISUALIZE scatter X Revenue Y Profit STAGE engineered
    TITLE "Revenue and Profit"
    X_LABEL "Revenue"
    Y_LABEL "Profit"
    THEME presentation
    COLOR "#059669"
    FIGSIZE "10,6"
    DPI 160
    GRID true;

# %% [Revenue histogram]
VISUALIZE histogram COLUMN Revenue STAGE engineered
    TITLE "Revenue Distribution"
    X_LABEL "Revenue"
    Y_LABEL "Transactions"
    THEME journal
    COLOR "#2563eb"
    FIGSIZE "10,6"
    DPI 160
    GRID true;

# %% [Profit boxplot]
VISUALIZE boxplot COLUMN Profit STAGE engineered
    TITLE "Profit Boxplot"
    Y_LABEL "Profit"
    THEME dark
    COLOR "#7c3aed"
    FIGSIZE "9,6"
    DPI 160
    GRID true;

# %% [Correlation heatmap]
VISUALIZE correlation_heatmap STAGE engineered
    TITLE "Engineered Feature Correlations"
    THEME journal
    PALETTE "viridis"
    FIGSIZE "12,9"
    DPI 180
    GRID false;

# %% [Customer age distribution]
VISUALIZE distribution COLUMN Customer_Age STAGE engineered
    TITLE "Customer Age Distribution"
    THEME light
    COLOR "#ea580c";

# %% [Quality score chart]
VISUALIZE quality_score STAGE current;

# %% [Missing-value chart]
VISUALIZE missing_values STAGE current;

# %% [Issue breakdown chart]
VISUALIZE issue_breakdown STAGE current;

# %% [Cleaning status chart]
VISUALIZE cleaning_status STAGE current;

# %% [Before and after comparison chart]
VISUALIZE comparison STAGE current;

# %% [markdown] 21. Manage the visualization gallery

Inspect, customize, save, and list reusable chart objects.

# %% [List all gallery charts]
GALLERY LIST;

# %% [Filter the gallery]
GALLERY LIST TYPE bar STAGE engineered;

# %% [Retrieve the regional chart]
GALLERY GET bar_Region_by_Revenue_engineered;

# %% [Customize the regional chart]
GALLERY CUSTOMIZE bar_Region_by_Revenue_engineered
    TITLE "Regional Revenue Performance"
    SUBTITLE "Average revenue after quality review"
    X_LABEL "Sales region"
    Y_LABEL "Average revenue"
    THEME journal
    PALETTE "cool"
    FIGSIZE "11,7"
    DPI 220
    GRID true
    LEGEND false
    LEGEND_POSITION best
    TEMPLATE publication
    TRANSPARENT false;

# %% [Save the visualization gallery]
GALLERY SAVE TO "../reports/sales_all/charts" FORMAT png;

# %% [List registered visualizations]
LIST VISUALIZATIONS;

# %% [markdown] 22. Train and persist a model

Train on engineered features while excluding likely identifiers and leakage.

# %% [Train the revenue model]
MODEL TARGET Revenue USING random_forest_regressor
    TEST_SIZE 0.20
    RANDOM_STATE 42
    USE_ENGINEERED true
    EXCLUDE_LEAKAGE true
    EXCLUDE Transaction_ID,Customer_ID;

# %% [Save the revenue model]
MODEL SAVE TO "../models/sales_all-revenue-model" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Reload the revenue model]
MODEL LOAD FROM "../models/sales_all-revenue-model";

# %% [markdown] 23. Predict with uncertainty

Generate point predictions, intervals, confidence metadata, and a reusable
prediction dataset.

# %% [Generate predictions]
PREDICT CONFIDENCE 0.90
    UNCERTAINTY true
    LOW_CONFIDENCE 0.60;

# %% [Retain predictions]
LET sales_predictions = PREDICTIONS OVERWRITE;

# %% [Inspect prediction intervals]
SELECT Transaction_ID,Region,Revenue,
       AutoDQ_Prediction,
       AutoDQ_Prediction_Lower,
       AutoDQ_Prediction_Upper,
       AutoDQ_Interval_Width,
       AutoDQ_Confidence_Level
FROM PREDICTIONS
ORDER BY AutoDQ_Prediction DESC
LIMIT 25;

# %% [markdown] 24. Explain the model with SHAP

Generate the structured explanation followed by each supported SHAP chart.

# %% [Explain representative predictions]
EXPLAIN MAX_ROWS 20 USE_ENGINEERED true;

# %% [SHAP summary plot]
SHAP CHART summary SAVE "../reports/sales_all/shap-summary.png";

# %% [SHAP importance bar plot]
SHAP CHART bar SAVE "../reports/sales_all/shap-bar.png";

# %% [SHAP beeswarm plot]
SHAP CHART beeswarm SAVE "../reports/sales_all/shap-beeswarm.png";

# %% [SHAP local waterfall plot]
SHAP CHART waterfall ROW 0
    SAVE "../reports/sales_all/shap-waterfall.png";

# %% [SHAP dependence plot]
SHAP CHART dependence FEATURE Customer_Age
    SAVE "../reports/sales_all/shap-customer-age.png";

# %% [markdown] 25. Run BLUE diagnostics

Evaluate linear-model assumptions, visualize diagnostics, explain their
meaning, and produce prescriptive recommendations.

# %% [Run BLUE diagnostics]
BLUE SOURCE data
    USE_ENGINEERED true
    EXCLUDE_LEAKAGE true
    MAX_FEATURES 12
    SIGNIFICANCE 0.05
    LEAKAGE_THRESHOLD 0.95
    EXCLUDE Transaction_ID,Customer_ID;

# %% [Visualize BLUE diagnostics]
BLUE VISUALIZE APPEND true ALLOW_DUPLICATES false;

# %% [Interpret BLUE diagnostics]
BLUE INTERPRET;

# %% [Prescribe BLUE improvements]
BLUE PRESCRIBE;

# %% [markdown] 26. Publish dashboards and reports

Build the presentation layer after quality, feature, model, SHAP, and BLUE
artifacts are available.

# %% [Generate the sales dashboard]
DASHBOARD
    TITLE "AutoDQ Complete Sales Analytics"
    SUBTITLE "Quality, cleaning, contracts, drift, features, modeling, SHAP, uncertainty, and BLUE diagnostics"
    THEME executive
    STAGE engineered
    MAX_CHARTS 20
    MAX_ROWS 25
    CHARTS true
    PREVIEW true
    REFRESH false
    DISPLAY false
    SAVE "../reports/sales_all/dashboard.html"
    OVERWRITE;

# %% [Generate the HTML report]
REPORT TO "../reports/sales_all/report.html"
    STYLE executive
    OVERWRITE;

# %% [Generate the JSON report]
REPORT TO "../reports/sales_all/report.json"
    STYLE executive
    OVERWRITE;

# %% [markdown] 27. Export reusable analysis artifacts

Export current, cleaned, engineered, prediction, summary, merged, and
concatenated datasets explicitly.

# %% [Export current and cleaned snapshots]
EXPORT CURRENT TO "../exports/sales_all-current.csv" OVERWRITE;
EXPORT cleaned_sales TO "../exports/sales_all-cleaned-snapshot.csv" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Export features and predictions]
EXPORT ENGINEERED TO "../exports/sales_all-features.xlsx" OVERWRITE;
EXPORT PREDICTIONS TO "../exports/sales_all-predictions.csv" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Export analytical summaries]
EXPORT regional_sales TO "../exports/sales_all-regional-summary.csv" OVERWRITE;
EXPORT sales_with_customers TO "../exports/sales_all-merged.csv" OVERWRITE;

# %% [Export concatenated sales]
EXPORT combined_sales TO "../exports/sales_all-concatenated.csv" OVERWRITE;

# %% [markdown] 28. Inspect workspaces and session history

These final read-only commands show persistent workspace inventory and the
state accumulated during this notebook run.

# %% [List persistent workspaces]
WORKSPACE LIST ROOT "../workspaces";

# %% [List workspaces through the common command]
LIST WORKSPACES;

# %% [Show the session summary]
SESSION;

# %% [Show recent session events]
SESSION EVENTS LIMIT 30;

# %% [Show session datasets]
SESSION DATASETS;

# %% [Show ADQL execution history]
HISTORY LIMIT 20;

# %% [markdown] Optional administrative and alternate strategies

The commands below are valid ADQL but are intentionally not executed during
the standard workflow because they create persistent workspaces, remove
gallery objects, or demonstrate mutually exclusive cleaning treatments.
Convert this Markdown cell to a code cell when you specifically need one.

```adql
WORKSPACE CREATE sales_all_workspace ROOT "../workspaces" TARGET Revenue;
WORKSPACE SAVE INCLUDE_MODEL true MODEL_NAME "sales_all-revenue-model";
WORKSPACE INFO;
WORKSPACE OPEN sales_all_workspace ROOT "../workspaces" LOAD_MODEL true;

GALLERY REMOVE boxplot_Profit_engineered;
GALLERY CLEAR;

MISSING FILL Revenue STRATEGY mean;
MISSING FILL Quantity STRATEGY zero;
MISSING FILL Region STRATEGY ffill;
MISSING FILL City STRATEGY bfill;

DUPLICATES DROP KEEP last;
